{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 658d10afaac1979d478db2b44d8d7abb703bd273, Mint lane A only. Both explicit implementation obligations are satisfied: the second conditional pre-send update durably stores the TTL and send time recomputed after the awaited wake; overdue times alone become now + 1 s, preserving still-future ledger times and the wake callback's earlier-alarm requirement. The supplied guards pass their independent controls, but two additional defects remain.\n\n[P1] Prevent credential-bearing provider errors from reaching durable duties — packages/git/src/mints.ts:122. The new message helper removes only art_v-shaped tokens before writing last_error or the observation result. The API accepts any nonempty plaintext as usable, so a minted opaque plaintext echoed in a failed revoke's Authorization: Bearer message is persisted and returned by duties(). My synthetic control mints a valid ID/scope/readable-expiry answer, verifies the returned plaintext, makes release fail with that bearer message, and then fails because JSON.stringify(duties()) contains the exact plaintext. No provider token-format restriction in the approved contract makes the regex sufficient. Use credential-aware, bounded error metadata or omit unsafe provider text; cover creation, revocation, repository acquisition and observation errors without a dependency from Git back to Room. The operator projection must preserve R-MINT-5's never-token-text boundary, including errors.\n\n[P1] Bound repository acquisition during observation and cleanup — packages/git/src/mints.ts:659 (also line 597). Both paths await repo() before entering within(). With repo() held, reconcile() never returns from observation, and the sole revocation pass never ends or writes its retry backoff; this.pass/observing prevent later attempts even when passUntil/observeUntil have elapsed. nextDue() then offers an overdue 1-second continuation while the actual work remains blocked indefinitely, and even already-expired owed records wait behind acquisition. Two independent controls with waitMs=10 remain pending after 60 ms, then finish only when I resolve the lookup. Bound acquisition as part of the relevant operation budget, record a failed attempt/backoff, release the in-flight marker, and ensure a late lookup cannot start stale provider work or mutate the settled attempt. R-MINT-7 and the report explicitly require an awaited observation bounded at 30 s and cleanup that cannot retain an unbounded pass.\n\nReported design choices: 1 (one transaction at pass end), 2 (known unusable answers owed to the next pass), 3 (backoff clamped to readable expiry), 6 (new unknowns advance due without resetting doubling), 7 (one indexed minimum/existence check/summary), 8 (additive test/idle/constants API and bounded full paging), and 9 (only retriable classes retry) preserve the approved lane contract. Choice 4 retains durable debt and the prior stored takeover wake if a later wake fails; the Room must still compose/store the next wake in lane B. Choice 5 accurately retains the earlier state when storage cannot record handoff/debt, as the approved design specifies; recovery may require a new object start and must remain explicit. These choices do not justify the unbounded repo() waits in the finding above. A takeover's single indexed update may be proportional to work in flight, as expressly allowed by the design; it does not scan the retained unknown history.\n\nArchitecture: the affected layer is the ordinary Artroom Git application/service library and its future Room integration. Gitseq storage, kernel, host and application-profile contracts are unchanged. This head adds four paths/updates only, leaves every production caller unchanged and preserves protocol section 32; no runtime integration or lane B/C behavior is approved here. One ledger with conditional row/state changes and transactional summary counts is the intended ownership boundary. The approved design ad6cc052 was independently reviewed, ratified and landed in 867e496c at main b803d210; the effective implementing request 1eda3c5e names that basis and both obligations. No new contract choice is silently adopted.\n\nSecurity: the effective planner-to-builder request, builder promise and all four artifacts were inspected and bind to this exact head; checker is independent. IDs are not reused, stale callbacks cannot change another owner, claim rolls back with its owner's transaction, unknown effects are retained and no inventory sweeping occurs. The extra synthetic tests establish a confidentiality failure and two availability/recovery failures, not a live credential disclosure. This request authorizes additive source and offline controls, not credential creation, deployment or provider operations.\n\nSimplification: keep the single ownership API, one shared observation and indexed paging; avoid per-record observation writes, blind sweeping and hidden non-idempotent retries. Apply one bounded operation helper to acquisition plus observation, and use a shared safe metadata boundary rather than another token-format-only redactor. These repairs preserve the full requested scope.\n\nIndependent validation at this exact head: clean detached /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1; npm ci, root typecheck and root npm test exit 0 (2,101 passed, 1 skipped; Room 138 Node and 403 workerd); Git test:workers exit 0, 10 passed; Room Wrangler 4.146.0 deploy --dry-run exit 0, no upload; git diff --check passes and checkout remains clean. Focused mint tests: 33 passed. In separate /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1-guards all 61 supplied mutants individually fail named runtime tests, zero syntax failures/survivors, then restored source passes all 33 with a clean checkout. The three extra controls fail on the unmodified candidate, with gates resolved afterwards so no pending lookup is abandoned. Script /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1-controls.ts; log /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1-controls.log. Mutation script /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1-mutants.py and results /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1-mut/mutants.json. Root/typecheck/worker/dry-run/restoration logs use the /tmp/artroom-checker-mint-a-v1- prefix.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:65cf0e437389f11436dcaa87eeec461790615e38","binding":"assigned","head":"658d10afaac1979d478db2b44d8d7abb703bd273","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c7d1ba1464129002da3fea12a46fed542d221ea2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b95cbbbd86b3dc7d7164e3607a99597691dc46a3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fed383b71752897032e127347bf0e4b0464d8937","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}